{
 "source": "plates_sheet.png",
 "_comment": "R9, the painted plates: green (confirm), red (danger) and navy (quiet) in five sizes (xl, l, m, s, xs; the navy's largest is the wide one) and the brick-red NO ENERGY face. Each is cut on its traced rim: keyed off the flat ground for its anti-aliased edge ('floor' drops the drop shadow's 14-24 of distance), held solid inside (a navy face is nearly ground-coloured), and masked to the octagon of its rim with its own chamfer, so its corners are clear. Drawn at 1:1 -- the xs plates are a 96-unit button's height -- and nine-patched only along their length. A surface with its own painting keeps that painting's plate (the Shop's BUY, the Army's HUNT, the Inventory's EQUIP and SELL, the Family's UPGRADE); these are for the rest: dialogs, Sheet feet, pages' extras.",
